* LT1720 Comparator Circuit

* 5V Supply
V1 VCC 0 5

* Input held above the 1.65V threshold
V2 IN 0 3

* Resistor divider setting the 1.65V threshold (5V * 33k / (67k + 33k) = 1.65V)
R1 VCC N001 67k
R2 N001 0 33k

* LT1720 Comparator (In+ In- V+ V- Out)
* Non-inverting input tied to threshold, inverting input tied to IN.
* Since IN (3V) > Threshold (1.65V), the output will be driven LOW (~0.0V).
X1 N001 IN VCC 0 OUT LT1720

* Open-drain style pull-up resistor to 5V
R3 OUT VCC 10k

* Analysis directive for DC/settled output measurement
.tran 1m

* Include standard comparator library
.lib cmp.lib

.end
